@testray.main.component.name = "Support QA"
@type = "koroneiki.provisioning.license.permission"

Feature:  Koroneiki To Licensing License Worker Permissions
	Testing to assure that provisioning license worker permissions work properly.

Setup:	
	* I create a provisioning user with the following parameters
	| Screen Name   | licensing.worker                    |
	| Email Address | licensing.worker@liferay.com.broken |
	| First Name    | Licensing                           |
	| Last Name     | Worker                              |
	* I assign the provisioning user with the email address "licensing.worker@liferay.com.broken" to the provisioning role "Provisioning Worker"

Teardown:
	* I wait for "5" seconds
	* I get the ID of the default user belonging to the organization "Perlic - ${staticProjectName}" from zendesk.liferay.com
	* I tear down the product consumption list on koroneiki made by the account "Perlic - ${staticProjectName}" for the following products
	| DXP Production |
	* I tear down the product purchases on koroneiki made by the account "Perlic - ${staticProjectName}" for the following products with their respective field values
	| DXP Production | startDate | ${staticStartDate}       |
	| DXP Production | startDate | ${staticFutureStartDate} |
	* I tear down the product purchases on koroneiki made by the account "Perlic - ${staticProjectName}" for the following products
	| DXP Production |
	* I tear down the accounts on koroneiki with the following names
	| Perlic - ${staticProjectName} |
	* I tear down the accounts on koroneiki with the following "Code" values
	| PERLICPERLIC |
	* I log out and log into the support homepage as "amos.fong@liferay.com.broken" with password "test"
	* I tear down the projects with the following project codes via groovy
	| PERLICPERLIC |
	* I wait for "5" seconds
	* I obtain the external IDs of the following organizations from zendesk.liferay.com
	| Perlic - ${staticProjectName} |
	* I teardown organizations with the following organizationExternalIds "${staticOrganizationExternalIdList}" from zendesk.liferay.com
	* I teardown the user with userId "${staticDefaultUserId}" from zendesk.liferay.com
	* I tear down the users with the following email addresses from provisioning
	| licensing.worker@liferay.com.broken |

Scenario: Generate new DXP license
	Testing the ability to generate a new license for a T4 DXP project from koroneiki on provisioning

	Given I generate a provisioning project name
	And I create an account on koroneiki with the following values
	| Code                  | PERLICPERLIC                         |
	| Contact Email Address | lic.koroneiki1@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| Description           | Test osb account on koroneiki        |
	| Fax Number            | 555-555-1234                         |
	| Name                  | Perlic - ${staticProjectName}        |
	| Phone Number          | 555-555-5678                         |
	| Profile Email Address | lic.koroneiki1@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| Region                | United States                        |
	| Status                | Active                               |
	| Tier                  | T4                                   |
	| Website               | www.koroneikicorporation.com         |
	And I generate the account key value for "Perlic - ${staticProjectName}"
	And I generate static start and end dates
	And I generate static full start and end dates
	And I generate future static start and end dates
	And I generate future static full start and end dates
	And I create a product purchase for an account with the name "Perlic - ${staticProjectName}" and the product "DXP Production" on koroneiki with the following values
	| End Date                | ${staticEndDate}         |   |
	| Original End Date       | ${staticOriginalEndDate} |   |
	| Perpetual               | false                    |   |
	| Product Field and Value | sizing                   | 1 |
	| Product Field and Value | licenses                 | 1 |
	| Product Field and Value | version                  | 7 |
	| Quantity                | 1                        |   |
	| Start Date              | ${staticStartDate}       |   |
	| Status                  | Approved                 |   |
	And I generate the product purchase ID value for the product purchase made by "Perlic - ${staticProjectName}" for "DXP Production"
	And I create a product purchase for an account with the name "Perlic - ${staticProjectName}" and the product "Platinum Subscription" on koroneiki with the following values
	| End Date                | ${staticEndDate}         | |
	| Original End Date       | ${staticOriginalEndDate} | |
	| Perpetual               | false                    | |
	| Quantity                | 1                        | |
	| Start Date              | ${staticStartDate}       | |
	| Status                  | Approved                 | |
	And I log into the provisioning homepage as "licensing.worker@liferay.com.broken" with password "provisioningqauser"
	And I update my password upon login to "test"
	And I go to the license index page
	And I click on the generate license button on the license index
	And I populate the generate license form with the following values
	| Account | Select Entity | Perlic - ${staticProjectName} | |
	| Product | Select        | DXP Production                | |
	| Version | Select        | 7.2                           | |
	| Type    | Select        | DXP Production (Production)   | |
	And I click on the choose button for the product purchase in position "1" on the license form
	And I populate the generate license form with the following values
	| Host Name     | Input    | localhost         | |
	| IP Addresses  | Textarea | 123.45.67.89      | |
	| MAC Addresses | Textarea | 0A-1B-2C-3D-4E-5F | |
	And I click on the generate button on the license form
	Then I should be able to view the following license values on the license page
	| Header  | Perlic - ${staticProjectName} | |
	| Product | DXP Production                | |
	When I go to the license index page
	And I search the licenses page using the keyword "${staticAccountKey}"
	Then I should be able to view a license on the provisioning index with the keyword "Perlic - ${staticProjectName}" and the following values
	| Name        | Perlic - ${staticProjectName}  |
	| Description | Perlic - ${staticProjectName}  |
	| Account     | Perlic - ${staticProjectName}  |
	| Product     | DXP Production                 |
	| Type        | Production                     |
	| Details     | Host Name: localhost           |
	| Details     | IP Address: 123.45.67.89       |
	| Details     | MAC Address: 0A-1B-2C-3D-4E-5F |
	When I click on the license with the keyword "Perlic - ${staticProjectName}" on the provisioning index
	Then I should be able to view the following license values on the license page
	| Header        | Perlic - ${staticProjectName} | |
	| Product       | DXP Production                | |
	| Version       | 7.2                           | |
	| Type          | Production                    | |
	| Host Name     | localhost                     | |
	| IP Addresses  | 123.45.67.89                  | |
	| MAC Addresses | 0A-1B-2C-3D-4E-5F             | |
	| Owner         | Perlic - ${staticProjectName} | |
	| Description   | Perlic - ${staticProjectName} | |
	| Complimentary | No                            | |
	| Status        | ACTIVE                        | |
	| Created By    | Licensing Worker              | |
	When I generate static infinite end dates
	And I generate static start dates
	And I should be able to view a product consumption on koroneiki made by the account "Perlic - ${staticProjectName}" for the product "DXP Production" with the following values
	| End Date   | ${staticInfiniteEndDates} | |
	| Start Date | ${staticStartDates}       | |
	When I go to the account index page
	And I search the accounts page using the keyword "Perlic"
	And I click on the account with the name "Perlic - ${staticProjectName}" on the provisioning index
	Then I should be able to view the product with the name "DXP Production" and the following values on the account details page
	| Name                | DXP Production |
	| Current Provisioned | 1              |
	| State               | ACTIVE         |
	When I click on the "DXP Production" subscription provisioned link
	Then I should be able to view the license with the keyword "Perlic - ${staticProjectName}" and the following values on the subscription details page
	| Name        | Perlic - ${staticProjectName}  |
	| Description | Perlic - ${staticProjectName}  |
	| Product     | DXP Production                 |
	| Type        | Production                     |
	| Details     | Host Name: localhost           |
	| Details     | IP Address: 123.45.67.89       |
	| Details     | MAC Address: 0A-1B-2C-3D-4E-5F |
	When I go to the account index page
	And I search the accounts page using the keyword "Perlic"
	And I click on the account with the name "Perlic - ${staticProjectName}" on the provisioning index
	And I click on the "DXP Production" subscription link
	And I click on subscription provisioned link
	Then I should be able to view the license with the keyword "Perlic - ${staticProjectName}" and the following values on the subscription details page
	| Name        | Perlic - ${staticProjectName}  |
	| Description | Perlic - ${staticProjectName}  |
	| Product     | DXP Production                 |
	| Type        | Production                     |
	| Details     | Host Name: localhost           |
	| Details     | IP Address: 123.45.67.89       |
	| Details     | MAC Address: 0A-1B-2C-3D-4E-5F |
	When I go to the account index page
	And I search the accounts page using the keyword "Perlic"
	And I click on the account with the name "Perlic - ${staticProjectName}" on the provisioning index
	And I click on the "DXP Production" subscription link
	And I click on provisioned link for the subscription term with the start date to end date "${staticFullStartDate} - ${staticFullEndDate}"
	Then I should be able to view the license with the keyword "Perlic - ${staticProjectName}" and the following values on the subscription details page
	| Name        | Perlic - ${staticProjectName}  |
	| Description | Perlic - ${staticProjectName}  |
	| Product     | DXP Production                 |
	| Type        | Production                     |
	| Details     | Host Name: localhost           |
	| Details     | IP Address: 123.45.67.89       |
	| Details     | MAC Address: 0A-1B-2C-3D-4E-5F |
	When I go to the account index page
	And I search the accounts page using the keyword "Perlic"
	And I click on the account with the name "Perlic - ${staticProjectName}" on the provisioning index
	And I click on the "Licenses" tab
	Then I should be able to view the license with the keyword "Perlic - ${staticProjectName}" and the following values on the account details page
	| Name        | Perlic - ${staticProjectName}  |
	| Description | Perlic - ${staticProjectName}  |
	| Product     | DXP Production                 |
	| Type        | Production                     |
	| Details     | Host Name: localhost           |
	| Details     | IP Address: 123.45.67.89       |
	| Details     | MAC Address: 0A-1B-2C-3D-4E-5F |
	And the "Active" license tab should have the count value "1"
	And the "Expired" license tab should have the count value "0"
	And the "Deactivated" license tab should have the count value "0"
	And the "All" license tab should have the count value "1"
	When I click on the "Expired" license tab
	Then I should not be able to view the license with the keyword "Perlic - ${staticProjectName}" on the account details page
	When I click on the "Deactivated" license tab
	Then I should not be able to view the license with the keyword "Perlic - ${staticProjectName}" on the account details page
	When I click on the "All" license tab
	Then I should be able to view the license with the keyword "Perlic - ${staticProjectName}" and the following values on the account details page
	| Name        | Perlic - ${staticProjectName}  |
	| Description | Perlic - ${staticProjectName}  |
	| Product     | DXP Production                 |
	| Type        | Production                     |
	| Details     | Host Name: localhost           |
	| Details     | IP Address: 123.45.67.89       |
	| Details     | MAC Address: 0A-1B-2C-3D-4E-5F |
	When I go to the account index page
	And I search the accounts page using the keyword "Perlic"
	And I click on the account with the name "Perlic - ${staticProjectName}" on the provisioning index
	And I click on the "DXP Production" subscription link
	And I click on the "Licenses" tab
	Then I should be able to view the license with the keyword "Perlic - ${staticProjectName}" and the following values on the subscription details page
	| Name        | Perlic - ${staticProjectName}  |
	| Description | Perlic - ${staticProjectName}  |
	| Product     | DXP Production                 |
	| Type        | Production                     |
	| Details     | Host Name: localhost           |
	| Details     | IP Address: 123.45.67.89       |
	| Details     | MAC Address: 0A-1B-2C-3D-4E-5F |
	And the "Active" license tab should have the count value "1"
	And the "Expired" license tab should have the count value "0"
	And the "Deactivated" license tab should have the count value "0"
	And the "All" license tab should have the count value "1"
	When I click on the "Expired" license tab
	Then I should not be able to view the license with the keyword "Perlic - ${staticProjectName}" on the subscription details page
	When I click on the "Deactivated" license tab
	Then I should not be able to view the license with the keyword "Perlic - ${staticProjectName}" on the subscription details page
	When I click on the "All" license tab
	Then I should be able to view the license with the keyword "Perlic - ${staticProjectName}" and the following values on the subscription details page
	| Name        | Perlic - ${staticProjectName}  |
	| Description | Perlic - ${staticProjectName}  |
	| Product     | DXP Production                 |
	| Type        | Production                     |
	| Details     | Host Name: localhost           |
	| Details     | IP Address: 123.45.67.89       |
	| Details     | MAC Address: 0A-1B-2C-3D-4E-5F |

Scenario: Generate new DXP license via account subscription
	Testing the ability to generate a new license for a T4 DXP project from koroneiki on provisioning via an account subscription

	Given I generate a provisioning project name
	And I create an account on koroneiki with the following values
	| Code                  | PERLICPERLIC                         |
	| Contact Email Address | lic.koroneiki1@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| Description           | Test osb account on koroneiki        |
	| Fax Number            | 555-555-1234                         |
	| Name                  | Perlic - ${staticProjectName}        |
	| Phone Number          | 555-555-5678                         |
	| Profile Email Address | lic.koroneiki1@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| Region                | United States                        |
	| Status                | Active                               |
	| Tier                  | T4                                   |
	| Website               | www.koroneikicorporation.com         |
	And I generate the account key value for "Perlic - ${staticProjectName}"
	And I generate static start and end dates
	And I generate static full start and end dates
	And I generate future static start and end dates
	And I generate future static full start and end dates
	And I create a product purchase for an account with the name "Perlic - ${staticProjectName}" and the product "DXP Production" on koroneiki with the following values
	| End Date                | ${staticEndDate}         |   |
	| Original End Date       | ${staticOriginalEndDate} |   |
	| Perpetual               | false                    |   |
	| Product Field and Value | sizing                   | 1 |
	| Product Field and Value | licenses                 | 1 |
	| Product Field and Value | version                  | 7 |
	| Quantity                | 1                        |   |
	| Start Date              | ${staticStartDate}       |   |
	| Status                  | Approved                 |   |
	And I generate the product purchase ID value for the product purchase made by "Perlic - ${staticProjectName}" for "DXP Production"
	And I create a product purchase for an account with the name "Perlic - ${staticProjectName}" and the product "Platinum Subscription" on koroneiki with the following values
	| End Date                | ${staticEndDate}         | |
	| Original End Date       | ${staticOriginalEndDate} | |
	| Perpetual               | false                    | |
	| Quantity                | 1                        | |
	| Start Date              | ${staticStartDate}       | |
	| Status                  | Approved                 | |
	And I log into the provisioning homepage as "licensing.worker@liferay.com.broken" with password "provisioningqauser"
	And I update my password upon login to "test"
	And I go to the account index page
	And I search the accounts page using the keyword "Perlic"
	And I click on the account with the name "Perlic - ${staticProjectName}" on the provisioning index
	And I click on the "DXP Production" subscription link
	And I click on generate license button on the subscription details page
	And I populate the generate license form with the following values
	| Product | Select | DXP Production              | |
	| Version | Select | 7.2                         | |
	| Type    | Select | DXP Production (Production) | |
	And I click on the choose button for the product purchase in position "1" on the license form
	And I populate the generate license form with the following values
	| Host Name     | Input    | localhost         | |
	| IP Addresses  | Textarea | 123.45.67.89      | |
	| MAC Addresses | Textarea | 0A-1B-2C-3D-4E-5F | |
	And I click on the generate button on the license form
	Then I should be able to view the following license values on the license page
	| Header  | Perlic - ${staticProjectName} | |
	| Product | DXP Production                | |
	When I go to the license index page
	And I search the licenses page using the keyword "${staticAccountKey}"
	Then I should be able to view a license on the provisioning index with the keyword "Perlic - ${staticProjectName}" and the following values
	| Name        | Perlic - ${staticProjectName}  |
	| Description | Perlic - ${staticProjectName}  |
	| Account     | Perlic - ${staticProjectName}  |
	| Product     | DXP Production                 |
	| Type        | Production                     |
	| Details     | Host Name: localhost           |
	| Details     | IP Address: 123.45.67.89       |
	| Details     | MAC Address: 0A-1B-2C-3D-4E-5F |
	When I click on the license with the keyword "Perlic - ${staticProjectName}" on the provisioning index
	Then I should be able to view the following license values on the license page
	| Header        | Perlic - ${staticProjectName} | |
	| Product       | DXP Production                | |
	| Version       | 7.2                           | |
	| Type          | Production                    | |
	| Host Name     | localhost                     | |
	| IP Addresses  | 123.45.67.89                  | |
	| MAC Addresses | 0A-1B-2C-3D-4E-5F             | |
	| Owner         | Perlic - ${staticProjectName} | |
	| Description   | Perlic - ${staticProjectName} | |
	| Complimentary | No                            | |
	| Status        | ACTIVE                        | |
	| Created By    | Licensing Worker              | |
	When I generate static infinite end dates
	And I generate static start dates
	And I should be able to view a product consumption on koroneiki made by the account "Perlic - ${staticProjectName}" for the product "DXP Production" with the following values
	| End Date   | ${staticInfiniteEndDates} | |
	| Start Date | ${staticStartDates}       | |

Scenario: Renew DXP license
	Testing the ability to renew a license for a T4 DXP project from koroneiki on provisioning

	Given I generate a provisioning project name
	And I create an account on koroneiki with the following values
	| Code                  | PERLICPERLIC                         |
	| Contact Email Address | lic.koroneiki1@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| Description           | Test osb account on koroneiki        |
	| Fax Number            | 555-555-1234                         |
	| Name                  | Perlic - ${staticProjectName}        |
	| Phone Number          | 555-555-5678                         |
	| Profile Email Address | lic.koroneiki1@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| Region                | United States                        |
	| Status                | Active                               |
	| Tier                  | T4                                   |
	| Website               | www.koroneikicorporation.com         |
	And I generate the account key value for "Perlic - ${staticProjectName}"
	And I generate static start and end dates
	And I generate static full start and end dates
	And I generate future static start and end dates
	And I generate future static full start and end dates
	And I generate future static yyyymmdd start and end dates
	And I create a product purchase for an account with the name "Perlic - ${staticProjectName}" and the product "Platinum Subscription" on koroneiki with the following values
	| End Date                | ${staticEndDate}         | |
	| Original End Date       | ${staticOriginalEndDate} | |
	| Perpetual               | false                    | |
	| Quantity                | 1                        | |
	| Start Date              | ${staticStartDate}       | |
	| Status                  | Approved                 | |
	And I log into the provisioning homepage as "licensing.worker@liferay.com.broken" with password "provisioningqauser"
	And I update my password upon login to "test"
	And I go to the license index page
	And I click on the generate license button on the license index
	And I populate the generate license form with the following values
	| Account | Select Entity | Perlic - ${staticProjectName} | |
	| Product | Select        | DXP Production                | |
	| Version | Select        | 7.2                           | |
	| Type    | Select        | DXP Production (Production)   | |
	And I click on the choose button for the product purchase in position "1" under the "Detached" section on the license form
	And I populate the generate license form with the following values
	| Host Name     | Input    | localhost         | |
	| IP Addresses  | Textarea | 123.45.67.89      | |
	| MAC Addresses | Textarea | 0A-1B-2C-3D-4E-5F | |
	And I click on the generate button on the license form
	Then I should be able to view the following license values on the license page
	| Header  | Perlic - ${staticProjectName} | |
	| Product | DXP Production                | |
	When I go to the license index page
	And I search the licenses page using the keyword "${staticAccountKey}"
	Then I should be able to view a license on the provisioning index with the keyword "Perlic - ${staticProjectName}" and the following values
	| Name        | Perlic - ${staticProjectName}  |
	| Description | Perlic - ${staticProjectName}  |
	| Account     | Perlic - ${staticProjectName}  |
	| Product     | DXP Production                 |
	| Type        | Production                     |
	| Details     | Host Name: localhost           |
	| Details     | IP Address: 123.45.67.89       |
	| Details     | MAC Address: 0A-1B-2C-3D-4E-5F |
	When I click on the license with the keyword "Perlic - ${staticProjectName}" on the provisioning index
	Then I should be able to view the following license values on the license page
	| Header        | Perlic - ${staticProjectName} | |
	| Product       | DXP Production                | |
	| Version       | 7.2                           | |
	| Type          | Production                    | |
	| Host Name     | localhost                     | |
	| IP Addresses  | 123.45.67.89                  | |
	| MAC Addresses | 0A-1B-2C-3D-4E-5F             | |
	| Owner         | Perlic - ${staticProjectName} | |
	| Description   | Perlic - ${staticProjectName} | |
	| Complimentary | No                            | |
	| Status        | ACTIVE                        | |
	| Created By    | Licensing Worker              | |
	When I click on the renew button for the license in position "1" on the license page
	And I populate the renew license form with the following values
	| Start Date      | ${staticYyyyMmDdFutureStartDate}       |
	| Expiration Date | ${staticYyyyMmDdFutureOriginalEndDate} |
	And I click on the renew button on the renew license form
	Then I should be able to view the following license values on the license page
	| Header        | Perlic - ${staticProjectName} | |
	| Product       | DXP Production                | |
	| Version       | 7.2                           | |
	| Type          | Production                    | |
	| Host Name     | localhost                     | |
	| IP Addresses  | 123.45.67.89                  | |
	| MAC Addresses | 0A-1B-2C-3D-4E-5F             | |
	| Owner         | Perlic - ${staticProjectName} | |
	| Description   | 365-Day License               | |
	| Complimentary | No                            | |
	| Status        | ACTIVE                        | |
	| Created By    | Licensing Worker              | |
	When I go to the account index page
	And I search the accounts page using the keyword "Perlic"
	And I click on the account with the name "Perlic - ${staticProjectName}" on the provisioning index
	And I click on the "Complimentary" product tab
	Then I should be able to view the product with the name "DXP Production" and the following values on the account details page
	| Name                | DXP Production |
	| Current Provisioned | 2              |
	| State               | -              |

Scenario: Bulk renew DXP licenses
	Testing the ability to bulk renew multiple new licenses for a T4 DXP project from koroneiki on provisioning

	Given I generate a provisioning project name
	And I create an account on koroneiki with the following values
	| Code                  | PERLICPERLIC                         |
	| Contact Email Address | lic.koroneiki1@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| Description           | Test osb account on koroneiki        |
	| Fax Number            | 555-555-1234                         |
	| Name                  | Perlic - ${staticProjectName}        |
	| Phone Number          | 555-555-5678                         |
	| Profile Email Address | lic.koroneiki1@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| Region                | United States                        |
	| Status                | Active                               |
	| Tier                  | T4                                   |
	| Website               | www.koroneikicorporation.com         |
	And I generate the account key value for "Perlic - ${staticProjectName}"
	And I generate static start and end dates
	And I generate static full start and end dates
	And I generate future static start and end dates
	And I generate future static full start and end dates
	And I generate future static yyyymmdd start and end dates
	And I create a product purchase for an account with the name "Perlic - ${staticProjectName}" and the product "DXP Production" on koroneiki with the following values
